From: LIVI OS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Prefer the GL core driver for OpenGL ES 3 builds

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LIVI graphics configuration]

The legacy gl driver is selected ahead of glcore when HAVE_OPENGLES is
enabled. In the GLES3 build it crashes during Wayland EGL initialization,
while glcore successfully creates an accelerated GLES3 context.

Prefer glcore when both GLES3 and the core driver are compiled in. Explicit
user driver settings and non-GLES3 builds retain their existing behaviour.

--- a/configuration.c
+++ b/configuration.c
@@ -436,6 +436,8 @@
 static const enum video_driver_enum VIDEO_DEFAULT_DRIVER = VIDEO_GL1;
 #elif defined(HAVE_VITA2D)
 static const enum video_driver_enum VIDEO_DEFAULT_DRIVER = VIDEO_VITA2D;
+#elif defined(HAVE_OPENGLES3) && defined(HAVE_OPENGL_CORE)
+static const enum video_driver_enum VIDEO_DEFAULT_DRIVER = VIDEO_GL_CORE;
 #elif defined(HAVE_OPENGL) || defined(HAVE_OPENGLES) || defined(HAVE_PSGL)
 static const enum video_driver_enum VIDEO_DEFAULT_DRIVER = VIDEO_GL;
 #elif defined(HAVE_OPENGL_CORE) && !defined(__HAIKU__)
